{
  "_comment": [
    "5E complication packages, structured — the disadvantage half of a Low Powered build (100 of",
    "its 250). Authored from the legacy prose in complications.5e.json, which stated each as a",
    "description with a hand-typed cost ('PsyL: Code Of The Hero (Very Common/Strong)', 20).",
    "",
    "As with the powersets, NO cost is stated here: the engine prices each from its adders. A",
    "disadvantage's cost is the sum of its adder basecosts — PSYCHOLOGICALLIMITATION is basecost 0",
    "with a SITUATION adder (Uncommon 5 / Common 10 / Very Common 15) and an INTENSITY adder",
    "(Moderate 0 / Strong 5 / Total 10), so Very Common + Strong is 20. The `input` field carries",
    "the description ('Code Of The Hero'); `optionid` is recorded for fidelity but the basecost is",
    "what prices.",
    "",
    "Shape is a .hdc `disadvantages` block, sub-key `disad`. Verified against the level's",
    "disadvantage limit in core/random/__tests__/complications.test.ts — every package must total",
    "exactly 100, which is what makes the legacy set a coherent Low Powered build.",
    "",
    "See docs/RANDOM_CHARACTER.md."
  ],
